# Negative-control mutant — the HARD cancel submit validates before it writes (AC-6, R33/R35)
#
# Scenario it must flip: the cancellation form's HARD path
#   (`processing.requestingCancellation`) runs `validating`
#   (`validateCancellation`) BEFORE `updating`, so an invalid model lands in the
#   form's `error` node and NO `cancel/request` POST leaves the module (R35's
#   own-processing form shape). (Re-authored: the pre-R33 single write region
#   this patch once targeted moved with R33; the cancelling region is the
#   contract product's now.)
# Test that goes red: NONE EXISTS YET for the HARD path. The AC-6 invalid->422
#   test (`contract-product.mutations.int.test.ts`) drives the SCHEDULE_FUTURE
#   option, whose control is
#   `contract-product.mutations.cancellation-invalid-model.must-fail.patch`; no
#   test submits an INVALID model under the HARD option and asserts the 422
#   lands with no POST. This is a GAP, surfaced not hidden (the developer seat
#   does not author tests; handed to the prover). Applying this patch and
#   running the sibling spec stays GREEN today — the proof of the gap. Once the
#   prover lands a HARD-option invalid-model test, that test is the one this
#   mutant must flip red.
# Mutation: `requestingCancellation.validating` routes its `onError` straight to
#   `updating` instead of the form's `#cancelling.available.error` node — the
#   invalid model is POSTed anyway.
#
# Apply with:  git apply <this file>   (run from repo root)
# Revert with: git apply -R <this file>
diff --git a/packages/headless/src/modules/contract-product/contract-product.machine.ts b/packages/headless/src/modules/contract-product/contract-product.machine.ts
index 86220f7bf..04c08d02c 100644
--- a/packages/headless/src/modules/contract-product/contract-product.machine.ts
